{"_id":"69e6382f31e228f31bc91fd0","roadmapSlug":"leetcode","nodeId":"zIpM4hiGUSXwkokZFRzSB","description":"# Sliding Window Maximum\n\nGiven an array and a window size k, return the maximum value in each window. A monotonic deque stores indices in decreasing order of value, so the front is always the current maximum. This problem teaches you the monotonic deque, which gives O(n) window max where a heap would give O(n log n).","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Sliding Window Maximum","url":"https://leetcode.com/problems/sliding-window-maximum/","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7ac2"},{"type":"video","title":"Sliding Window Maximum (LeetCode 239)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WcTMo1SHV_s","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7ac3"},{"type":"video","title":"Sliding Window Maximum: Efficient  Solution","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5VjQD62gOYA","_id":"6a60910cfcaecc259f0e7ac4"}],"createdAt":"2026-04-20T14:29:03.248Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-22T09:44:44.827Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/leetcode/content/zIpM4hiGUSXwkokZFRzSB.md"}